read_details.py        read a --details table with numpy; RC range and tail fractions per spectrum
plot_rc.C              ROOT macro: RC factor and tail fractions of one spectrum from the --root tree
engine_from_csv.cpp    use the library from C++: read any input format, drive the engine directly
                       (built as build/engine_from_csv)
python_unfold.py       unfold spectra given as numpy arrays with python/radcor.py
mini/                  the two-spectrum example of the manual, chapter "Input and output files"

Convert inputs between formats with the command line, e.g.
  build/radcor convert unpol --dir data/e94010/unpol --to e94010.csv
